<node id="Tòa Án">
  <data key="d0">Tòa Án</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Tòa Án is a court of law that resolves disputes and makes decisions related to land use and ownership. As a competent authority, Tòa Án has the power to settle disputes and issue verdicts or decisions regarding land-related matters, including the ownership of construction projects and the right to use land. Specifically, Tòa Án is responsible for issuing judgments and decisions related to the acquisition of land use rights. Additionally, Tòa Án serves as a judicial body with the authority to resolve land-related disputes, complaints, and denunciations. Overall, Tòa Án plays a crucial role in addressing land-related issues and ensuring that the rights of individuals and organizations are protected and upheld.&lt;SEP&gt;Tòa Án is a court that resolves land disputes and has the authority to make decisions on land use and ownership.&lt;SEP&gt;Tòa Án is a court that resolves land disputes and has the authority to make decisions on land use and ownership.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-441a092bb7fe3b39b917ede05c2b268f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a50678dc89e78c25b96d5730912275a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939c3d1ca63be7c24c9dbe48ca6a3c0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab00d1578ba42cbe5a546e3b79f1ddbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdffa592834f59c1831a91e8118b491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0430c7cc3f6209ae0492f4d5eb6ccb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d0a130dde5b2a8f28df5fbfd9026e1d</data>
