<node id="Điều 176">
  <data key="d0">Điều 176</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Điều 176 is a regulatory article that outlines the conditions for land use rights, specifically dealing with land allocation and use for rice cultivation and other agricultural purposes. It is a part of the law that governs land use, focusing on the limits of land allocation for agricultural use, including the maximum amount of land that can be allocated for farming. The article provides guidelines on land use rights, ensuring that land is utilized efficiently and effectively for agricultural activities such as rice cultivation. Overall, Điều 176 plays a crucial role in regulating land use and allocation, providing a framework for the management of agricultural land in accordance with the law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2e528eb6259d26484885d9a6e60fbee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e95fa72656913e44897b9372de39ee00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d0ee27e69be940ef4f753775a5c0e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb91494ba903a6cbf58dd04a909a74f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b9cd51d144c28bf97ce93d074263e35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52e88b1840bd8e004eb0f5e24c9f7e53</data>
